      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the review job this clone has no copy of the patch set, so the checkout on the next line fails.\n\n`actions/checkout` fetches main at depth 1, so the workspace is shallow. Git won\u0027t clone a shallow repository locally: it ignores `--shared`, writes no `alternates`, and fetches only branches and `HEAD`, not `refs/review/patchset`. I set up a copy the way the job does (main at depth 1, the patch set fetched at depth 2 into `refs/review/patchset`) and ran the recipe:\n\n```\n$ git -C \"$scratch\" checkout -q --detach 6857a890e77f8ff3236f7458319e74d1d7d24579\nfatal: reference is not a tree: 6857a890e77f8ff3236f7458319e74d1d7d24579\n```\n\nSo every probe starts with a failure that Muse has to get round. The easy way round is to check out `REV` in the working tree. The skill forbids that, and it puts the change\u0027s own `render-session.py` in front of the Render step (see gerrit-verify.yml:386).\n\nFix: `git worktree add -q --detach \"$scratch\" REV` works on the shallow repository and shares its objects. I ran it, and it gives 6857a89 on 8c7b120. Remove it afterwards with `git worktree remove --force \"$scratch\"`. Fetching the ref into the clone before the checkout also works: `git -C \"$scratch\" fetch -q \"$repo\" refs/review/patchset`.",
