      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gerrit refuses an inline comment on a file the patch set doesn\u0027t change, and the whole review with it.\n\nGerrit\u0027s `CommentsValidator` checks each comment\u0027s path against the files the revision changes. One miss fails the whole request with 400: `file \u003cpath\u003e not found in revision`. The Worker then answers 502, `curl -f` fails, and nothing is posted, after the review has been paid for. \"One finding per comment, on the line where it happens\" leads to exactly this. Typical cases are a caller the change didn\u0027t update, or `check.yml`\u0027s copy of the list that gerrit-verify.yml says must match. Two more cases fail the same way:\n\n- A reply to a `/PATCHSET_LEVEL` thread has no line. The Worker sends `line: 0`, and Gerrit refuses that with `Patchset-level comments can\u0027t have side, range, or line`. This one is gerrithub-ci\u0027s to fix: leave `line` out when none was given.\n- The skill doesn\u0027t say where commit-message findings (rule 5) go. Gerrit\u0027s `/COMMIT_MSG` starts with a `Parent:`/`Author:`/`Commit:` header, so its line numbers aren\u0027t those of `git log -1 --format\u003d%B`.\n\nFix: tell the skill to put new comments only on files `git diff --name-only REV^ REV` lists, or on `/COMMIT_MSG` with that header taken into account. Anything else goes in the summary. Then have the Post step enforce it by moving any other comment into the summary, so one stray path can\u0027t sink the review.",
      "revId": "6857a890e77f8ff3236f7458319e74d1d7d24579",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
