      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not blocking: when a fetch fails, this step fails instead of falling back.\n\nWithout a `shell`, a step runs `bash -e` with no `pipefail`. So `get` returns `tail`\u0027s status, and `comments\u003d$(get comments)` succeeds with empty output. `jq --argjson comments \"\"` then fails, and `-e` ends the step. I ran the step with a change number that doesn\u0027t exist:\n\n```\ncurl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 404\njq: invalid JSON text passed to --argjson\nexit\u003d2\n```\n\nA brief Gerrit outage would therefore fail the job, not review without the history as the warning says.\n\nFix: `shell: bash` (that adds `pipefail`), and move the `jq` into the `if` condition, so bad JSON falls back as well.",
      "revId": "6857a890e77f8ff3236f7458319e74d1d7d24579",
